Atlas overlay patch 0020: ui/default-vertical
Why: the window opens with the tabs in a 220 px sidebar (reel scene R02, patches-0 P-06). The layout
pref `helium.browser.layout` registers with the vertical value as its default, so every profile that
never chose a layout gets the sidebar, and the default sidebar width becomes 220 px (the width
constant also drives the resize snap, so dragging snaps back to 220). A first-run pref only reaches
new profiles and would store an explicit value, which is why the registered default changes.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/tabs/tab_strip_prefs.cc, chrome/browser/ui/tabs/vertical_tab_strip_state.h
Test filter: *VerticalTabStripStateController*; journey R02 (sidebar width 220 +-2)
Rebase risk: L (two one-line edits in files the inherited layout patch already changed)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
